# Python and text file quality

These rules prevent compressed single-line files and Unicode warnings on GitHub.

## Python source

- Write normal multiline Python source files
- Never write an entire module on one line
- Each import statement on its own line (or a clear parenthesized group)
- Each class, function, and method uses normal newlines and indentation
- Keep lines reasonably short; target max line length under 140 characters

## Markdown and MDC

- Use normal multiline Markdown
- Never compress a whole document into one line
- Use ASCII punctuation in project rules and docs when possible
  - Prefer hyphen-minus (-) over em dash
  - Prefer -> over Unicode arrows

## Unicode

- Do not introduce hidden or bidirectional Unicode characters
- Avoid zero-width spaces and direction override characters
- Prefer UTF-8 plain text with visible ASCII where sufficient

## After Python edits

- Run: python -m pytest
- Fix failures before opening or updating a PR
